          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"workers-kv-analytics\">Workers KV analytics</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will explore KV logs, where we will make use of the GraphQL API to obtain KV insights\nand rank entries by most requests, whether they are <code>read</code>, <code>write</code> and <code>list</code> requests.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><b style='color: tomato'>Warning:</b> by default this notebook will fetch at most 500 KV entries from a given\naccount, whilst other entries will be grouped into an \"Other\" entry. This number can be increased by\nincreasing the <code>_MAX_PAGE_REQUESTS</code> variable, which dictates how many hundreds of KV name - Id pairs\nare obtained from the API.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/create-token/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>\nfor info on how to create one);<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- At least one active KV.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
